,"default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null},{"id":370471880,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWwzNzA0NzE4ODA=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/labels/topic:physics","name":"topic:physics","color":"ffee88","default":false,"description":"","archived_at":null,"archived_by":null}],"state":"closed","locked":false,"assignees":[],"milestone":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/milestone/25","labels_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/milestones/25/labels","id":15520464,"node_id":"MI_kwDOAO6SJc4A7NLQ","number":25,"title":"4.8","description":"","creator":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"open_issues":345,"closed_issues":2336,"state":"open","created_at":"2026-04-13T15:59:35Z","updated_at":"2026-10-22T08:21:32Z","due_on":null,"closed_at":null},"comments":1,"created_at":"2026-10-01T13:30:51Z","updated_at":"2026-10-16T16:38:18Z","closed_at":"2026-10-16T16:38:12Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"MEMBER","issue_field_values":[],"type":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/124062","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124062","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124062.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/124062.patch","merged_at":"2026-10-16T16:38:12Z"},"body":"## What problem(s) does this PR solve?\r\n\r\nReduces the code size of the GodotPhysics2D SAT by 70%, and 30% for the 3D SAT, by reducing some template parameters combinatorial explosion, especially in 2D. In 2D, we go from 8 template instantiations per shape combination down to 1.\r\n\r\nI evaluated binary size gains on `template_release` binaries as:\r\n- 1.50 MiB for Linux GCC LTO (2.00%). That's 0.89 MiB for the first commit and 0.61 MiB for the second commit.\r\n- 0.92 MiB for Linux Clang ThinLTO (1.18%), respectively 0.58 MiB and 0.34 MiB for the individual commits.\r\n- 725 KiB for Web .wasm (2.20%), 148 KiB when gzipped, 63 KiB when Brotli-compressed.\r\n\r\n## Additional information\r\n\r\nI let AI build and run some throwaway synthetic physics tests and micro-benchmarks to confirm that the simulation remains identical.\r\n\r\n### Performance\r\n\r\nI ran before/after tests on https://github.com/godotengine/godot-benchmarks/tree/main/benchmarks/physics to see if our benchmarks measure any noticeable performance loss. Sadly there was a lot of noise from these benchmarks, with ±10-20% across runs so it wasn't usable to track a potential small performance impact.\r\n\r\nI had AI generate a micro benchmark for the 2D SAT and it found 5-10% performance regression from those two commits, most of it from the first commit (moving the two cast parameters to runtime). So I tested adding back one template parameter `withCast` to at least mitigate impact in the no-collision case, but that only regained part of the performance.\r\n\r\nThen I checked how much impact the SAT can be expected to have on a physics step and estimated it to ~30% in a worse case scenario (profiling 1200 2D shapes of different types colliding with each other).\r\n\r\nFinally I compared performance using https://github.com/godotengine/godot-demo-projects/tree/master/2d/physics_tests/tests/performance (modified to work headlessly and stress the physics more) and could measure no performance difference, just ~1% noise.\r\n\r\nSo overall, I think this change is relatively safe. It does impact performance in a somewhat hot path, but overall the impact seems small and worth it for a 70% code size reduction.\r\n","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124062/reactions","total_count":11,"+1":2,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":4,"confused":0,"heart":2,"rocket":2,"eyes":1},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/124062/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}